Scope of this license, and third-party material

1. New contributions of this work -- the `csr/` directory, `docs/`,
   `results/`, `scripts/`, and the top-level build files (`reproduce.sh`,
   `requirements*.txt`, `Dockerfile`, `README.md`, `CITATION.cff`,
   `RELEASE_NOTES.md`) -- are released under the MIT License above.

2. Upstream-derived files -- `models/`, `datasets/`, `runners/`,
   `optimizers/`, `config/`, `data/`, `train.py`, `utils.py`, `vocab.py` --
   are copied from the official PC-Net repository
   (https://github.com/mingyao1120/PC-Net, NeurIPS 2025). **That repository
   ships no LICENSE file**, so this package grants no license for those files
   beyond what their authors permit; they are included solely so that the
   released numbers can be reproduced. Copyright remains with the original
   authors (see `docs/UPSTREAM_VERIFICATION.md`).

3. `models/modules/net_vlad.py` is code by Antoine Miech, licensed under the
   Apache License 2.0; its header is kept verbatim. Files under `optimizers/`
   derive from fairseq and carry Facebook copyright headers (MIT).

4. Model checkpoints distributed as GitHub Release assets are provided for
   research reproduction only.

5. If you are an upstream author and want the derived files removed from this
   repository, please open an issue; they will be dropped and replaced by a
   setup script that copies them from upstream.
